= Finite Dimensional Vector Spaces

== Summary

This chapter builds upon the previous chapter to limit the scope of discussion to finite dimensional vector spaces. The main concepts one needs to understand in this chapter are linear independence and span in my opinion, and then building on top of that there is basis. After that the author touched on the definition of dimension.

I would say spend some time going through the definitions and implications of linear independence and span, then the results in basis and dimension should be fairly straightforward.

Overall I think this chapter is important as it introduces the notion of linear independence and span, but it could get a bit plain after that. As the author pointed out in the following chapter: no one gets excited about vector spaces.

== Key questions
  - What is the definition of linear independence?
  - What is span?
  - What is a basis?
  - What is definition of dimension?
  
